# g75-fu-screen-displays: the desktop half.

1. apps/desktop/src/main/host/index.ts, in registerHostMethods beside `registerScreenDisplaysHost(...)` (hot file): call
   `const stopDisplayReports = reportScreenDisplayChanges(connection, screen);` (`screen` from 'electron'; `reportScreenDisplayChanges` and
   `HOST_SCREEN_DISPLAYS_CHANGED` are exported by ./screen-displays, added by this task with its test) and call `stopDisplayReports()`
   in the connection's close handler. It sends the notification `host/screen/displaysChanged` {} (the rows are in
   pending-rows/g75-fu-screen-displays.rows).
2. apps/desktop/src/main/computer/host/display-reads.ts (s3-31's, not edited here), `readDisplays()`: add `label: display.label,` to each
   entry (the OS's name for the monitor, which the phone's picker lists; the core's `ReportedDisplay` reads it, an older desktop without it
   falls back to "Display N").
3. After x-screen-source-desktop, `host/screen/displays` is no longer asked of the desktop (the core lists the monitors itself): its handler
   registerScreenDisplaysHost may be deleted by that task's follow-up together with the `remoteScreenDisplays` browser path.
